---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DraftNotice from "../components/DraftNotice.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms of use for this insurance education and comparison site."
>
  <DraftNotice
    note="These draft terms have not been reviewed by a lawyer and are not a final or binding legal agreement. Do not treat this page as legal advice or a substitute for a lawyer-drafted terms of use."
  />
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      By using this site, you agree to the terms below. This is a draft and
      will be replaced with a lawyer-reviewed version before this site is
      used publicly.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      This site provides general, educational information about U.S. car and
      home insurance. [Legal entity name] is not an insurance company, and is
      not a licensed insurance agent or broker in any state unless separately
      stated. Nothing on this site is insurance advice, a quote, an offer to
      sell insurance, or a coverage decision.
    </p>

    <h2>No professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Information on this site — including state rules, coverage
      explanations, and results from tools like the Coverage Gap Checker — is
      general and educational. It does not account for your specific policy
      language, which controls over anything shown here. Always confirm
      anything important with your insurer or a licensed insurance
      professional before making a coverage decision.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We verify facts against primary sources — regulators, government
      bodies, or an insurer's own published terms — and show a source link
      and a "last verified" date for each one. Even so, laws and insurer
      practices change, and we cannot guarantee that every fact is current or
      error-free. If something here conflicts with your insurer's policy
      language or your state's current law, the policy language and current
      law control.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <p>
      Tools on this site, including the Coverage Gap Checker, produce
      educational output based only on what you type in. They do not see
      your actual policy, do not rate risk, do not recommend a company, and
      do not compare prices. Output from these tools is not a substitute for
      reviewing your declarations page or speaking with a licensed
      professional.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty; limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      This site is provided "as is," without warranties of any kind. To the
      fullest extent permitted by law, [Legal entity name] is not liable for
      decisions made based on information or tools on this site. [This
      section requires review by a lawyer before publication — limitation of
      liability language is jurisdiction-specific.]
    </p>

    <h2>Content ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Text, design, and tools on this site belong to [Legal entity name]
      unless otherwise noted. Facts and figures traced to a government or
      regulator source remain that source's information; we cite it rather
      than claim ownership of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms as the site develops. Continued use of the
      site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>[To be determined with legal counsel.]</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>[Contact details to be added once a legal entity and contact process are established.]</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
